---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="How It Works — AVS AUTH">
  <Header />
  <main class="docs-page container">
    <div class="docs-header">
      <a href="/docs" class="back-link">&larr; Back to Docs</a>
      <span class="section-label">GUIDE</span>
      <h1 class="docs-title">How It Works</h1>
    </div>

    <article class="doc-article">
      <section class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="doc-heading">The Big Picture</h2>
        <p>
          AVS AUTH is an <strong>authentication broker</strong>. It sits between your app and an
          identity provider (Google). Instead of each app integrating Google OAuth directly, apps
          delegate authentication to the broker.
        </p>
        <p>
          The key innovation: every app gets a <strong>pairwise subject ID</strong> for each user.
          This means apps cannot correlate users across different origins. User privacy is
          preserved by design.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="doc-heading">The Flow</h2>
        <div class="flow-diagram">
          <div class="flow-step">
            <div class="flow-num">1</div>
            <div class="flow-content">
              <h3>Authorization Request</h3>
              <p>
                Your app redirects the user to <code>/authorize</code> with a PKCE code challenge
                (S256), a redirect URI, and state parameter. No client registration — your origin
                IS the client ID.
              </p>
              <pre class="doc-code"><code>GET /authorize
  ?response_type=code
  &redirect_uri=https://yourapp.com/auth/callback
  &code_challenge=E9Melhoa2OwvFrEMTJguCHaoeK1t8URW...
  &code_challenge_method=S256
  &state=random_state_value</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flow-step">
            <div class="flow-num">2</div>
            <div class="flow-content">
              <h3>User Authentication</h3>
              <p>
                If the user has no active broker session, they sign in via Google.
                If they already have a session (cookie), this step is skipped entirely.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flow-step">
            <div class="flow-num">3</div>
            <div class="flow-content">
              <h3>User Consent</h3>
              <p>
                First time only: the user sees a consent screen showing your app's origin and
                what data is being requested. PII (email, name, picture) requires explicit
                opt-in. Consent can be revoked per-site.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flow-step">
            <div class="flow-num">4</div>
            <div class="flow-content">
              <h3>Authorization Code</h3>
              <p>
                The broker redirects back to your app with a short-lived authorization code.
              </p>
              <pre class="doc-code"><code>302 https://yourapp.com/auth/callback
  ?code=abc123
  &state=random_state_value</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flow-step">
            <div class="flow-num">5</div>
            <div class="flow-content">
              <h3>Token Exchange</h3>
              <p>
                Your app exchanges the code + PKCE verifier for an <code>id_token</code>.
                The token is signed with ES256 and contains a pairwise subject unique to your
                origin.
              </p>
              <pre class="doc-code"><code>POST /token
Content-Type: application/json
{"{"} "code": "abc123", "code_verifier": "dBjftJeZ4CVP-mB92K27..." {"}"}

→ {"{"} "id_token": "eyJhbGciOiJFUzI1NiIs..." {"}"}</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="doc-heading">Token Claims</h2>
        <pre class="doc-code"><code>{"{"}<br/>  "iss": "https://auth.adityavs.tech",<br/>  "aud": "origin:https://yourapp.com",<br/>  "sub": "pairwise_unique_id",<br/>  "pairwise_sub": "pairwise_unique_id",<br/>  "iat": 1712000000,<br/>  "exp": 1712086400,<br/>  "jti": "unique_token_id",<br/>  "email": "user@example.com",    // only if PII consent<br/>  "name": "User Name",            // only if PII consent<br/>  "picture": "https://..."         // only if PII consent<br/>{"}"}</code></pre>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="doc-heading">Session Management</h2>
        <p>
          The SDK includes built-in session monitoring. After sign-in, it periodically
          checks <code>/session/check</code> to detect revoked or expired sessions.
        </p>
        <p>
          When a <code>login_required</code> response is received, the monitor automatically
          stops polling. The session state transitions to <code>login_required</code> and
          local identity is cleared.
        </p>
        <pre class="doc-code"><code>POST /session/check

→ {"{"} "status": "active" {"}"}
→ {"{"} "status": "login_required", "reason": "expired" {"}"}</code></pre>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section">
        <h2 class="doc-heading">Privacy Model</h2>
        <p>
          The <code>sub</code> claim is derived using HMAC-SHA256 with a per-origin key.
          Two different apps will never see the same subject ID for the same user.
          This prevents cross-origin user tracking.
        </p>
        <p>
          PII fields (email, name, picture) are only included if the user explicitly
          grants PII consent for that specific origin. This consent is revocable.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .docs-page {
    padding-top: 40px;
    padding-bottom: 60px;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .back-link {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--yellow);
    opacity: 0.6;
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    transition: opacity var(--transition);
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .docs-header {
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .section-label {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--yellow);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .docs-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .doc-article {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .doc-section {
    padding-bottom: 40px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .doc-section:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .doc-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .doc-section p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    opacity: 0.65;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .doc-section strong {
    color: var(--white);
  }

  .doc-section code {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    background: rgba(235, 255, 0, 0.08);
    color: var(--yellow);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  .doc-code {
    background: rgba(245, 245, 245, 0.03);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 16px 20px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    overflow-x: auto;
    color: var(--yellow);
    margin: 12px 0;
  }

  .doc-code code {
    background: none;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--yellow);
  }

  /* Flow diagram */
  .flow-diagram {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .flow-step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 48px 1fr;
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 24px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .flow-step:first-child {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .flow-num {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--yellow);
    opacity: 0.5;
    padding-top: 2px;
  }

  .flow-content h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
</style>
